/*
 * pricewatch.c — Danish grocery price aggregator in a single C file.
 *
 * Collects real product prices from Danish supermarkets, stores every observation
 * in SQLite (price history), and finds the cheapest products / a cheapest basket
 * for a recipe like a pizza.
 *
 * Dependencies: libcurl + sqlite3 (both ship with macOS and are standard on Linux).
 * A tiny JSON parser is embedded, so there is no cJSON dependency.
 *
 * BUILD
 *     cc -O2 -o pricewatch pricewatch.c -lcurl -lsqlite3
 *   (macOS needs the Command Line Tools; Linux: apt install libcurl4-openssl-dev libsqlite3-dev)
 *
 * SOURCES
 *   salling   Official API (Netto, føtex, Bilka). Needs SALLING_TOKEN env var.
 *   rema1000  REMA 1000 app backend (unofficial). This week's advertised products.
 *   tjek      Tjek / eTilbudsavis offers for many DK chains. --dk-grocery = DK grocery only.
 *
 * ⚠️  Only Salling is an official API. REMA/Tjek use undocumented endpoints: fine for
 *     personal/educational use at low rates; check each source's terms before
 *     commercial or large-scale use.
 *
 * USAGE
 *     export SALLING_TOKEN=...                        # optional, only for `salling`
 *     ./pricewatch scrape --source tjek --dk-grocery
 *     ./pricewatch scrape --source rema1000
 *     ./pricewatch scrape --source salling --zip 8000
 *     ./pricewatch latest --query mælk
 *     ./pricewatch basket pizza
 *     ./pricewatch basket mel,mozzarella,tomat,pepperoni
 *     ./pricewatch dealers --dk-grocery
 *     ./pricewatch history --ean 5700002327239
 */
